    "solution": "Catch the lower carriage and let its rail stop at the held gate. Pay out onto the broad station plate below; it briefly restarts the train. Leave an echo on the plate before reeling away, so the gate stays open as the train carries you out. Shorten the rope, then jump-release into the independently moving upper carriage when it comes alongside. The higher rail supplies the final approach to the east gallery.",
    "nearestExisting": "F37 Catch the Other Train is an open two-carriage handoff. F19 The Weight Must Stay leaves an echo as a launch weight; this room instead interrupts the lower train and makes the knight give up that attachment before arranging a new rendezvous with an independently moving upper train.",
    "novelty": "The platform is first a locked station lift and later the lower half of a moving transfer. Arriving on the plate starts the train leaving: the echo must preserve that permission while the knight reels back up. The meeting with the independently moving upper train is downstream of this spatial preparation.",
